        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91039605?u=fdb24bedc39f5bdef7c6a0791bd2da2053800cb4&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Hello,</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43017.\">Fix</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3898337393\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43017\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43017/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43017\">#43017</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For the file -&gt; files/en-us/web/api/url/href/index.md</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Added a second example to the URL href docs that shows when the logged URL has a trailing slash (origin-only URLs like <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org</a>), and linked to the pathname docs for the full explanation.</li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thank you 😊.</p>",
